HHIISSTTOORRYY
     The aalltteerraa__ssddccaarrdd device driver first appeared in FreeBSD 10.0.

AAUUTTHHOORRSS
     The aalltteerraa__ssddccaarrdd device driver and this manual page were developed by
     SRI International and the University of Cambridge Computer Laboratory un‐
     der DARPA/AFRL contract (FA8750-10-C-0237) (“CTSRD”), as part of the
     DARPA CRASH research programme.  This device driver was written by Robert
     N. M. Watson.

BBUUGGSS
     aalltteerraa__ssddccaarrdd contains a number of work-arounds for IP core bugs.  Per‐
     haps most critically, aalltteerraa__ssddccaarrdd ignores the CRC error bit returned in
     the RR1 register, which appears to be unexpectedly set by the IP core.

     aalltteerraa__ssddccaarrdd uses fixed polling intervals are used for card inser‐
     tion/removal and I/O completion detection; an adaptive strategy might im‐
     prove performance by reducing the latency to detecting completed I/O.
     However, in our experiments, using polling rates greater than 200 times a
     second did not improve performance.

     aalltteerraa__ssddccaarrdd supports only a nexus bus attachment, which is appropriate
     for system-on-chip busses such as Altera's Avalon bus.  If the IP core is
     configured off of another bus type, then additional bus attachments will
     be required.

